### POS System: end-to-end walkthrough for the IntelliJ HTTP Client (run the requests top to bottom).
### Pick the "local" environment in the top right of the editor. Everything goes through the gateway.

### 1. Log in as the administrator of the demo company DEFAULT (the "tenant" is the company code; token is stored)
POST {{gateway}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tenant": "DEFAULT", "username": "admin", "password": "Admin#12345" }

> {% client.global.set("token", response.body.accessToken); %}

### 2. Who am I?
GET {{gateway}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3. Create a cashier for the main store (store 1 is created by the database seed)
POST {{gateway}}/api/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "cashier1",
  "password": "Cashier#1234",
  "fullName": "Cora Cashier",
  "storeId": 1,
  "roles": ["CASHIER"],
  "pin": "1234"
}

### 4. Create a product (category 1 = General and tax rate 1 = VAT 12% inclusive are seeded)
POST {{gateway}}/api/catalog/products
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sku": "COFFEE-001",
  "barcode": "4800000000011",
  "name": "Brewed Coffee 12oz",
  "categoryId": 1,
  "taxRateId": 1,
  "price": 120.00,
  "cost": 35.00
}

> {% client.global.set("productId", response.body.id); %}

### 5. Add stock to the main store
POST {{gateway}}/api/inventory/receive
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "storeId": 1, "productId": {{productId}}, "quantity": 50, "note": "Opening stock" }

### 6. Set the low-stock threshold (a notification is queued when stock falls to this level)
PUT {{gateway}}/api/inventory/stock/reorder-level
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "storeId": 1, "productId": {{productId}}, "reorderLevel": 10 }

### 7. Open a shift on terminal 1 with a 1,000.00 cash float
POST {{gateway}}/api/sales/shifts/open
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "storeId": 1, "terminalId": 1, "openingCash": 1000.00 }

> {% client.global.set("shiftId", response.body.id); %}

### 8. Ring up a sale (clientRef makes retries safe: sending the same value again returns the same sale)
POST {{gateway}}/api/sales
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "clientRef": "{{$uuid}}",
  "storeId": 1,
  "terminalId": 1,
  "lines": [ { "productId": {{productId}}, "quantity": 2 } ]
}

> {% client.global.set("saleId", response.body.sale.id); %}

### 9. Check out: pay 240.00 with a 500.00 note (the change is 260.00)
POST {{gateway}}/api/sales/{{saleId}}/checkout
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "payments": [ { "method": "CASH", "amount": 500.00 } ] }

### 10. Print the receipt
GET {{gateway}}/api/sales/{{saleId}}/receipt
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 11. Stock was deducted asynchronously through Kafka (give it a second)
GET {{gateway}}/api/inventory/stock?storeId=1&productId={{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 12. Refund one unit (supervisor level; cash back to the customer)
POST {{gateway}}/api/sales/{{saleId}}/refund
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Customer changed mind", "method": "CASH", "restock": true, "lines": [ { "saleLineId": 1, "quantity": 1 } ] }

### 13. X-read: the shift report while the shift is still open
GET {{gateway}}/api/sales/shifts/{{shiftId}}/x-read
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 14. Z-read: close the shift with the counted cash (variance = counted - expected)
POST {{gateway}}/api/sales/shifts/{{shiftId}}/close
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "countedCash": 1120.00 }

### 15. Sales summary for today (the report is built from events, so it lags by a moment)
< {% request.variables.set("today", new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10)); %}
GET {{gateway}}/api/reports/sales/summary?from={{today}}&to={{today}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 16. Cashier fast login with a PIN (what the till uses)
POST {{gateway}}/api/auth/pin-login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tenant": "DEFAULT", "username": "cashier1", "pin": "1234" }

### 17. Queued notifications (low stock, goods received)
GET {{gateway}}/api/notifications
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 18. Create a promotion: buy 2 get 1 free on the product, store 1 only, automatic (no coupon)
POST {{gateway}}/api/catalog/promotions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "COFFEE-B2G1", "name": "Buy 2 get 1 free", "type": "BUY_X_GET_Y",
  "buyQty": 2, "getQty": 1, "productId": {{productId}}, "storeId": 1 }

### 19. Create a coupon promotion: 15.00 off per unit, only when the cashier enters WELCOME20, needs 2 or more units
POST {{gateway}}/api/catalog/promotions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "WELCOME", "name": "Welcome coupon", "type": "FIXED", "value": 15.00,
  "minQty": 2, "couponCode": "WELCOME20", "endsAt": "2030-12-31T00:00:00Z" }

### 20. Ring up 3 coffees with the coupon (buy-2-get-1 and the coupon compete: the larger discount wins, they do not stack)
POST {{gateway}}/api/sales
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "clientRef": "{{$uuid}}", "storeId": 1, "terminalId": 1, "couponCodes": ["WELCOME20"],
  "lines": [ { "productId": {{productId}}, "quantity": 3 } ] }

### 21. Supervisor-only: override the tax of one line with a tax object (zero-rated here). The tax object is optional.
POST {{gateway}}/api/sales
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "clientRef": "{{$uuid}}", "storeId": 1, "terminalId": 1,
  "lines": [ { "productId": {{productId}}, "quantity": 1,
               "tax": { "code": "EXEMPT", "rate": 0, "inclusive": true } } ] }

### 22. A product now shows its tax as one optional object (tax is null for an untaxed product)
GET {{gateway}}/api/catalog/products/{{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 23. Sign out: the token is revoked immediately (the next request with it returns 401)
POST {{gateway}}/api/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 24. Force a user off every device (manager/admin): all their tokens stop working
POST {{gateway}}/api/users/2/sign-out
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ======================= Multiple companies (tenants), each with its own stores =======================
### Steps 25 onward: the platform operator creates a client company; that company's administrator sets up its
### own stores, catalog and users. Companies never see each other's data.

### 25. Log in as the platform operator (no "tenant"; first start creates platform / Platform#12345)
POST {{gateway}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "platform", "password": "Platform#12345" }

> {% client.global.set("platformToken", response.body.accessToken); %}

### 26. Create a client company with its first administrator
POST {{gateway}}/api/platform/tenants
Authorization: Bearer {{platformToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "ACME", "name": "Acme Retail Inc.", "adminUsername": "boss", "adminPassword": "Boss#12345" }

> {% client.global.set("tenantId", response.body.id); %}

### 27. List companies
GET {{gateway}}/api/platform/tenants
Authorization: Bearer {{platformToken}}

### 28. Log in as the new company's administrator
POST {{gateway}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tenant": "ACME", "username": "boss", "password": "Boss#12345" }

> {% client.global.set("acmeToken", response.body.accessToken); %}

### 29. The company starts empty: create its first store (ids are global; use the id in the response)
POST {{gateway}}/api/admin/stores
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "MAIN", "name": "Acme Flagship" }

> {% client.global.set("acmeStoreId", response.body.id); %}

### 30. A second store (a company can have as many as it needs; the code only has to be unique within the company)
POST {{gateway}}/api/admin/stores
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "NORTH", "name": "Acme North" }

### 31. Its own catalog: tax rate, category and product (same SKUs as other companies are fine)
POST {{gateway}}/api/catalog/tax-rates
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "VAT", "name": "VAT 12%", "rate": 12, "inclusive": true }

> {% client.global.set("acmeTaxId", response.body.id); %}

###
POST {{gateway}}/api/catalog/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "General" }

> {% client.global.set("acmeCategoryId", response.body.id); %}

###
POST {{gateway}}/api/catalog/products
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sku": "COFFEE-001", "name": "Brewed Coffee 12oz", "categoryId": {{acmeCategoryId}},
  "taxRateId": {{acmeTaxId}}, "price": 99.00 }

### 32. Isolation: ACME sees only its own product; the DEFAULT company's product ({{productId}}) is a 404 for ACME
GET {{gateway}}/api/catalog/products?q=COFFEE
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}

###
GET {{gateway}}/api/catalog/products/{{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}

### 33. The platform operator manages companies but owns no business data (an empty list or 403, never a company's products)
GET {{gateway}}/api/catalog/products
Authorization: Bearer {{platformToken}}

### 34. Suspend a company: nobody can log in and everybody signed in is signed out at once
POST {{gateway}}/api/platform/tenants/{{tenantId}}/suspend
Authorization: Bearer {{platformToken}}

### 35. The suspended company's token no longer works (401) and logging in is refused (403)
GET {{gateway}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}

### 36. Reactivate it
POST {{gateway}}/api/platform/tenants/{{tenantId}}/activate
Authorization: Bearer {{platformToken}}
